## The rule (fixed before grading)

- A decision is a **clear mistake** only when the whole 95% interval of what it cost you is above zero. You made 5 clear mistakes in all.
- A kind of decision is a **leak** only with at least 5 clear mistakes, in at least 3 different games, and an average cost over all your decisions of that kind whose 95% interval is above zero. Anything else is "not shown": not proof that you play it well, only that these games do not show a pattern.

